{
  "_why": "Role track for PLC / AUTOMATION, a new trade (CEO Launch Plan Pack v1, Phase 2 #6, sheet 14). fam_plc_automation binds NCO 7412.0101 'Automation Specialist' (maintenance of process-control systems on the shop floor) at job-domain specificity 50; every other 7412 code stays on fam_electrical_equipment and the industrial electrician keeps 7412.0200.",
  "_scope": "PROGRAMMING AND TROUBLESHOOTING AUTOMATION, NOT PANEL WIRING. Sheet 14 / A3: an electrician who only wires PLC panels is an Industrial Electrician; a worker whose main job is reading, editing or writing ladder logic, HMI/SCADA, drives and commissioning is this trade. The ladder's lowest rung (panel wiring and I/O checks under an engineer) is still here, because that is where the trade starts.",
  "_depth": "THE TIER GATE IS plc_experience, asked FIRST. Its options carry value_number ONLY: pack-registry.service.ts resolves valueText ?? valueNumber, and a value_text would turn every gte below into a string compare that is false forever (the #776 defect).",
  "_budget": "MAX_ENGINE_ASKS is 28 and qp_universal spends 8. Easy is 2 trade items + at most 1 confirm (each confirm is asked only of its own rungs); Medium adds 2 (PLC brand, work); Advanced adds 3 (HMI/SCADA, industry, field devices). Worst case 2 + 1 + 2 + 3 = 8 trade asks.",
  "_sheet": "READ OFF CEO LAUNCH PLAN PACK v1 SHEET 14 (a new trade, no ratified page). Section title 'Automation, PLC & capability'. Its rows are PLC brands, Work done, HMI/SCADA, Industry and Field devices, and every row has exactly one question here.",
  "pack_id": "qp_plc_automation",
  "version": 1,
  "family_id": "fam_plc_automation",
  "locale": "hi-IN",
  "status": "active",
  "review_note": "v1 (CEO Launch Plan Pack v1, Phase 2 #6): new trade. Easy/Medium/Advanced tiers; 6-band experience; sheet-14 level ladder (Trainee/Technician/Senior technician/Lead/Supervisor, mandatory); 2 separating confirms, the sheet's questions: technician (verbatim), and senior technician (the sheet's two questions joined into one — the runtime refuses a prompt with two question marks; same content) (also asked of lead by the standing owner rule of 2026-11-03 — the sheet writes none for lead); supervisor by rule. Medium Q6 PLC brand, Q7 work done; Advanced Q9 HMI/SCADA, Q10 industry, Q11 field devices, gated years OR rung. Deviations recorded: the sheet prices technician Higher, but rung tiers are per KEY across trades and the maintenance and electrician sheets rule `technician` Lower — the tier hook only logs today, so the shared key stands and a per-pack tier override is a follow-up; the technician confirm still confirms. No fresher items and no per-trade ITI row (Q12 is the shared qp_universal block; 3D CAD precedent for a new trade). The HMI brand chips beyond the sheet's own words (WinCC, FactoryTalk) are the common Indian-shop panels, for curator review. Drafted for owner review (Prakash).",
